---
subject: Security alert: your Detag session was reused

--- text ---
Hi,

A sign-in session on your Detag account was used in a way that looks like theft — the same session token was presented twice. As a precaution, all of your sessions were signed out.

If this was you (for example, a browser restoring an old tab), just sign in again. If it was not you, change your password after signing in.

— The Detag team

--- html ---
<!doctype html>
<html>
  <body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#f6f6f6;">
    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="background:#f6f6f6;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center">
          <table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="background:#ffffff;margin:24px 0;padding:32px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222222;">
            <tr>
              <td>
                <p>Hi,</p>
                <p>A sign-in session on your Detag account was used in a way that looks like theft — the same session token was presented twice. As a precaution, all of your sessions were signed out.</p>
                <p>If this was you (for example, a browser restoring an old tab), just sign in again. If it was not you, change your password after signing in.</p>
                <p>— The Detag team</p>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
